    {
      "id": "A1-04-l2",
      "position": 2,
      "skill": "grammar",
      "title": "there is / there are",
      "est_minutes": 25,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "markdown_ar": "نستخدم **there is** و **there are** لنقول إن شيئاً **موجود** في مكان («يوجد»).\n\n- **There is** + اسم مفرد: There is **a** board.\n- **There are** + اسم جمع: There are **thirty** chairs.\n- المختصر: **There's** a book."
        },
        {
          "type": "video",
          "youtube_id": "m8VUaW1b_z8",
          "video_title": "كلمات المنزل والفصل — الحلقة 4",
          "channel": "ZAmericanEnglish",
          "channel_url": "https://www.youtube.com/@ZAmericanEnglish",
          "duration_sec": 657,
          "optional": true,
          "approx_size_mb": 44
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "الحالة",
            "المفرد",
            "الجمع"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "إثبات",
              "There is a lab.",
              "There are two labs."
            ],
            [
              "نفي",
              "There isn't a library.",
              "There aren't any windows."
            ],
            [
              "سؤال",
              "Is there a lab?",
              "Are there any books?"
            ],
            [
              "إجابة",
              "Yes, there is. / No, there isn't.",
              "Yes, there are. / No, there aren't."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "markdown_ar": "**a أم an؟** نستخدم **an** قبل الكلمة التي تبدأ بصوت حرف علة (a, e, i, o, u): **an** English book, **an** office. وغير ذلك **a**: **a** desk, **a** pen.\n\n**الجمع:** نضيف **s** غالباً: book ← books. وبعد s و sh و ch و x نضيف **es**: class ← classes. وبعض الكلمات شاذة: man ← men, woman ← women, child ← children."
        },
